Content:
@RebelMike You know what, if you're not opposed to the idea, let's use TQVE as a guinea pig "die that actually does something interesting" for flip chip bonding, after the `FC01` connectivity test has done good work.
Idea/plan would be to run the flex away from the pad edge towards the die center and have the flex PCB's coverlay come up between center of the die and the die edge that the traces will then run over, so that this potential issue edge is kept isolated despite the exposed pad metal on the sealring there.
It will need quite fine alignment though, so not for the start/early-trials, IMO.
